{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules","id":997085,"title":"Some questions on blurry rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-02T04:55:35-07:00","id":997085,"title":"Some questions on blurry rules","content":"Hi guys, i just wanted to ask u and have ur opinion regarding the messi rules found in the 20th anniversary edition (bear in mind that english is not my first language so i apologize in advance)<br /> <br /> I think i understand the basic rules for instant casting and effects that come into play right away- a fireball inflicts damage according to the chart, and a healing spells heals &quot;x&quot; damage.<br /> <br /> I also understand the mechanics for rituals and extended casting and the dividing successes option-<br /> <br /> However i have some doubts<br /> <br /> 1) if i'm a life mage shapechanger, and say i want to change my appearence to look like another person or i want to grow fangs and claws, i need life 3 and three successes.<br /> <i>Do the total amount of successes count toward the duration too? </i>Say i roll three successes with my arete roll, do i transform into the new form for one entire day since i have three successes?<br /> <br /> 2) Same thing regarding mind control. If i roll three successes and say to someone i've maybe already influenced or is my ally &quot;protect me!&quot; and i score three successes, does that mean that he will protect me for the entire day? (according to the chart and the duration)<br /> <br /> 3) Same question for the physical boost of attributes- if i score 3 successes on my arete roll, and i boost my dexterity by three points, will this change last for an entire day or do i need to spend more successes beyond the basic successes for extended duration? (rules for extended casting and instant seems to blur here)<br /> <br /> ----it seems to me that UNLESS u use the extended casting and optional dividing success rule spells that require three successes or more will basically last for days or even the entire story by default when u score a good arete roll. Am i missing something here? <br /> <br /> 4)If i use time acceleration and score 5 successes on my arete roll, i will have 2 extra actions every turn for six months? (5 successes, duration chart)-<br /> <br /> ----On adjusting the arete difficulty roll.<br /> <br /> it says that the cap for every modifier cannot exceed the -3, howerver there is a smal paragraph that explain that by spending extra quintessence its possible to cancel out extra modifier for the difficulty on the casting- so for example:<br /> <br /> 5)if i want to travel back in time one or two rounds (vulgar without witnesses), i add +3 to the standard difficulty, raising the difficulty up to 10. Can i spend 3 points of quintessence to cancel out that +3 for time rewinding and THEN use a focus or something else to lower the difficulty even more?<br /> for example i set a small ritual or use my unique and focused instrument, lowering the difficulty to -3, and then i spend 3 quintessence points to cancel the +3 difficulty to the time rewind factor?<br /> <br /> 6) time travel also seems like a bitch to understand to me. If i go back in time or rewind an entire scene <i>do my character have memories of what had just happened in the present/future or does he need mind 2 to store the memory and change the scene? If so, if my mage doesn't have mind sphere dots, do we simply re-replay the entire scene and nothing changes? (since he doesn't know or remember which choices he made in the future and cannot change the time flow)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance if u try to clear up this mess for me, i'm trying to setup a mage campaign for beginner players, and i dont want to mess it up ^^ its a problem if even the storyteller doesn't have clear ideas on the rules and the setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:40:38-07:00","id":997130,"title":"","content":"On questions 1 to 4 you are right. You count your total successes once against the task at, and once again against the duration. This is true if:<br /> a) you do not do damage(or healing)<br /> b) you do not use the optipnal divided successes rule<br /> <br /> Regarding question 4)<br /> You are right, but you age 18 months also.<br /> <br /> 5) yes this is possible (and even encouraged to have a chance at some difficult feats)<br /> Your difficulty can not deviate by more than 3 from the base difficulty.<br /> Example:<br /> You use Forces 2 to turn invisible while no sleeper is watching you.<br /> Base difficulty is 2 (Forces rank used) + 4 (vulgar without witnesses) = 6<br /> Now we assume you are under pressure and have to fast-cast (+1)<br /> We assume further that you have major trouble with your avatar (+3)<br /> There is a mage casting antimagick with 3 successes (+3)<br /> <br /> Final difficulty in this case would be 9 and not 6+1+3+3=13 because the cap is at +3 and 6+3=9.<br /> <br /> Now for some modifiers in your favour.<br /> <br /> Same situation as aboove plus<br /> - you fortunately have Avatar 5 and spend 5 quintessence (-5)<br /> - there is a node nearby with resonances perfectly with your spell (-3)<br /> - you use your unique and personal invisibility cloak (-2)<br /> <br /> Now we have 6+1+3+3-5-3-2=3<br /> <br /> Even if you would use abilities enhancing magick the difficulty wouldn't go lower.<br /> <br /> The Time Travel is indeed very blurry.<br /> <br /> Of the top of my head:<br /> If you use Time alone then you keep your conditions (wounds, knowledge, paradox) from before the spell.<br /> Other spheres come in handy if you don't want damage to travel with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":"forgotten) 11-02-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:27:02-07:00","id":997193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=997130#post997130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On questions 1 to 4 you are right. You count your total successes once against the task at, and once again against the duration. This is true if:<br /> a) you do not do damage(or healing)<br /> b) you do not use the optipnal divided successes rule<br /> <br /> Regarding question 4)<br /> You are right, but you age 18 months also.<br /> <br /> 5) yes this is possible (and even encouraged to have a chance at some difficult feats)<br /> Your difficulty can not deviate by more than 3 from the base difficulty.<br /> Example:<br /> You use Forces 2 to turn invisible while no sleeper is watching you.<br /> Base difficulty is 2 (Forces rank used) + 4 (vulgar without witnesses) = 6<br /> Now we assume you are under pressure and have to fast-cast (+1)<br /> We assume further that you have major trouble with your avatar (+3)<br /> There is a mage casting antimagick with 3 successes (+3)<br /> <br /> Final difficulty in this case would be 9 and not 6+1+3+3=13 because the cap is at +3 and 6+3=9.<br /> <br /> Now for some modifiers in your favour.<br /> <br /> Same situation as aboove plus<br /> - you fortunately have Avatar 5 and spend 5 quintessence (-5)<br /> - there is a node nearby with resonances perfectly with your spell (-3)<br /> - you use your unique and personal invisibility cloak (-2)<br /> <br /> Now we have 6+1+3+3-5-3-2=3<br /> <br /> Even if you would use abilities enhancing magick the difficulty wouldn't go lower.<br /> <br /> The Time Travel is indeed very blurry.<br /> <br /> Of the top of my head:<br /> If you use Time alone then you keep your conditions (wounds, knowledge, paradox) from before the spell.<br /> Other spheres come in handy if you don't want damage to travel with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, thank u so much for replying. Second I really like your idea on time travel and the combination of other spheres. That way I could use both time and life for examples to travel back and cancel out my wounds too or reverse aging, or use prime to cancel put paradox or other magical conditions I experienced.<br /> Make sense!<br /> <br /> On the other hand, do u think it would be possible to allow for a player to use entropy 3 and time 3 to go back in time and choose another possible future?<br /> <br /> In an actual play, after the casting I allow the player to &quot;simulate&quot; one possible turn every two successes, and then he can choose which one unravel in the actual time.. what do u think? According to the handbook it's possible to combine both entropy and time to glimpse possible futures and choose one among them.<br /> <br /> Of corse it would be mighty feat really hard to pull off and really vulgar requiring 5 or more successes... and paradox magnet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:35:22-07:00","id":997200,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4247_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4247\" data-vbnamecard=\"4247\">Lasombra</a> I think it possible, it is nothing other than control probability applied to the past. If the alteration in question could be done with Entropy 3 back then, then you quite possibly can do it afterwards by adding Time to the mix.<br /> <br /> By the way, one cool rote from 2nd i think was the Wonderful Forgivenesd of Pope Honorious (or something like that)<br /> Time and Prime at Masterlevel and you can nullify paradox you don't have...yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:30:34-07:00","id":997225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=997200#post997200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <br /> <br /> By the way, one cool rote from 2nd i think was the Wonderful Forgivenesd of Pope Honorious (or something like that)<br /> Time and Prime at Masterlevel and you can nullify paradox you don't have...yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok that sounds god awfully broken and powerplay XD but I guess that's what one would expect from a master of that level xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:38:57-07:00","id":997231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=997200#post997200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;4247&quot;]you can nullify paradox you don't have...yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>My head just exploded trying to think about this (I have my computer set to send messages when/if my head were to ever explode).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:08:20-07:00","id":997327,"title":"","content":"Another crazy idea on time sphere- what about mashing mind and time together to send &quot;messages&quot; or telepathy signals from the future? After I had a car crash, I could send telepathically through time a message to myself (possibly.using correspondence if the location of my past self is out of my reach) saying that I sould not go drive that day.<br /> <br /> I could also transfer my conscience or thoughts in the future or the past.<br /> <br /> But now there's another issue- can time allow u to cast spells back and forth through time itself? Scary thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:14:39-07:00","id":997397,"title":"","content":"Possibly, but M20 introduced layered Paradox to cope with Time savvy Mages.<br /> 6 dox per turn you fling your fireball backwards in time sounds not ideal.<br /> And you have to deal with Disbelief, possibly counters and other symptoms of a displeased ST...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:03:58-07:00","id":997673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=997130#post997130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On questions 1 to 4 you are right. You count your total successes once against the task at, and once again against the duration. This is true if:<br /> a) you do not do damage(or healing)<br /> b) you do not use the optipnal divided successes rule<br /> <br /> Regarding question 4)<br /> You are right, but you age 18 months also.<br /> <br /> 5) yes this is possible (and even encouraged to have a chance at some difficult feats)<br /> Your difficulty can not deviate by more than 3 from the base difficulty.<br /> Example:<br /> You use Forces 2 to turn invisible while no sleeper is watching you.<br /> Base difficulty is 2 (Forces rank used) + 4 (vulgar without witnesses) = 6<br /> Now we assume you are under pressure and have to fast-cast (+1)<br /> We assume further that you have major trouble with your avatar (+3)<br /> There is a mage casting antimagick with 3 successes (+3)<br /> <br /> Final difficulty in this case would be 9 and not 6+1+3+3=13 because the cap is at +3 and 6+3=9.<br /> <br /> Now for some modifiers in your favour.<br /> <br /> Same situation as aboove plus<br /> - you fortunately have Avatar 5 and spend 5 quintessence (-5)<br /> - there is a node nearby with resonances perfectly with your spell (-3)<br /> - you use your unique and personal invisibility cloak (-2)<br /> <br /> Now we have 6+1+3+3-5-3-2=3<br /> <br /> Even if you would use abilities enhancing magick the difficulty wouldn't go lower.<br /> <br /> The Time Travel is indeed very blurry.<br /> <br /> Of the top of my head:<br /> If you use Time alone then you keep your conditions (wounds, knowledge, paradox) from before the spell.<br /> Other spheres come in handy if you don't want damage to travel with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may, can you provide a page reference so I could get a better idea of points 1 through 5 with counting successes once against the affect and again against the duration? I was under the impression that you basically required extended time and casting in order for effects to last for long durations, and that successes beyond what you need minimum for the effect went toward increasing the duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:15:48-07:00","id":997677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20; p. 502</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damage or Duration for these feats (not both at once) are based upon the number of successes rolled, as per the Base Damage or Duration chart. If you chose Damage, then Duration is instant. If you choose Duration, then Damage is zero<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Beloe the table with magickal feats.<br /> <br /> In revised and under the optional divided successes rule you have to score successes separately for each category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T13:56:04-07:00","id":998425,"title":"","content":"Since we're on the subject of time ( which is a mind f*** for me as a ST ), how does it work exactly with going back? I mean if we have a cabal of 3 mages, a scene where one dies, and on this very round one mages things 'screw this, this is not how it was supposed to go'' and casts time travel : past. Now, does it mean the dead mage is ressurected and they all go back to desired place in time? Or does the said mage stays dead and the rest goes back in time? Or is it just the time mage that goes back and I am now stuck in 2 time flowsohgodHELP ME UNDERSTAND THIS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T14:51:30-07:00","id":998447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=998425#post998425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're on the subject of time ( which is a mind f*** for me as a ST ), how does it work exactly with going back? I mean if we have a cabal of 3 mages, a scene where one dies, and on this very round one mages things 'screw this, this is not how it was supposed to go'' and casts time travel : past. Now, does it mean the dead mage is ressurected and they all go back to desired place in time? Or does the said mage stays dead and the rest goes back in time? Or is it just the time mage that goes back and I am now stuck in 2 time flowsohgodHELP ME UNDERSTAND THIS</div> </div> </div> </div>First it requires Time 3 to step oneself back. Second if they are going back the need Life 3 Mind 1 to recall the now future events they are leaving otherwise they take the same actions they took before. Additionally effects that turn back time are always vulgar and suffer an additional +3 difficulty (maximum difficulty being 10 or 9 and requiring additional successes if using the threshold option) additionally it is a Difficult Feat to step out of time requiring three successes; every two successes allow the Mage to rewind one turn however each turn rewound adds a layer (multiplier) of Paradox (ex going back 3 turns means getting 3 times the Paradox incurred by the effect and even on a success vulgar magic incurs 1 paradox which would then become 3 if the Mage went back 3 turns).<br /> <br /> If your mage successfully goes back (with memory of the future events through Life 3 Mind 1) time will pick up and follow its path as it did previously until such a point that the time traveling Mage does something then the others will react to the new events breaking the previous timeline. So if the friend died during those turns the Mage could try to do something different to prevent it (for example if the friend is shot and killed the Mage could go back and attack the shooters before they could take the shot).<br /> <br /> Now if you wanted to have the Mage 'reboot' the dead friend back to life by rewinding body to a state from turns ago it requires Life 5 Mind 4 Time 3 due to working the intricacies of patterns and consciousness and added three additional successes required over any others (so over the 3 for the feat difficulty and the 2+ for rewinding the appropriate number of turns) for affecting another target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:04:12-07:00","id":998455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=998447#post998447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now if you wanted to have the Mage 'reboot' the dead friend back to life by rewinding body to a state from turns ago it requires Life 5 Mind 4 Time 3 due to working the intricacies of patterns and consciousness and added three additional successes required over any others (so over the 3 for the feat difficulty and the 2+ for rewinding the appropriate number of turns) for affecting another target.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's easier to go back few rounds before and avoid whatever killed his friend with just T3/L3/M1 so. Ok that makes some sense - I missed the part where it's crazy hard to go really far back in time - for some reason I pictured him going days back. It actually makes sense now cheers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:44:55-07:00","id":998576,"title":"","content":"Time 3 on its own should be enough. Only the Time mage has to go back in time, they don't have to bring anyone else with them. The story just follows their perspective and the other players will have no idea what just happened.<br /> <br /> I used to play a Time mage and this sort of stuff happened almost constantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T20:23:35-07:00","id":998588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=998576#post998576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 3 on its own should be enough. Only the Time mage has to go back in time, they don't have to bring anyone else with them. The story just follows their perspective and the other players will have no idea what just happened.<br /> <br /> I used to play a Time mage and this sort of stuff happened almost constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under Time 3 it specifically mentions requiring Life 3 Mind 1 to recall the events of the future they just came from. M20 pg 523<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Combining this Rank with other Spheres, the mage can affect other Patterns (Forces, Life, or Matter 2), cast Effects across distance and time (Correspondence 3), <b>move back in time while recalling events from the future she just left (Life 3/ Mind 1)</b>, or even invoke multiple probabilities (Entropy 3). Again, such attempts are Paradox magnets with awful longterm consequences. </div> </div> </div>And relevant parts from M20 How Do You Do That pg 111 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Time Loop: In this case, the mage turns time back upon itself within a certain area of effect. Story-wise, you might see Lee Ann cut a complex glyph in the air with her lotus sword; everything within the room stops moving except for Lee Ann herself, and then it all \u201crewinds\u201d to a given point in time while Lee Ann changes the actions she would have taken otherwise. In game terms, time loops count as Magickal Feats of Time, with bigger reversals becoming bigger feats. Repeated time-loops suffer the Repeated Time Effects penalty described above.<br /> <br /> Reboot: By adding Life 3 and Mind 1 to the Time 3 Time Warp, the mage can send herself back a few turns (or other increments of time) with full memories of what had happened before. In this case, the rest of the world moves exactly as it had moved before until and unless the mage changes the course of its actions. If, for example, Lee Ann goes back to stab a cultist before he fires at her friend Kyle, then the cultist (and Kyle) respond to her \u201crebooted\u201d actions. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T20:39:15-07:00","id":998591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=998588#post998588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Under Time 3 it specifically mentions requiring Life 3 Mind 1 to recall the events of the future they just came from. M20 pg 523</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be really dumb if it was the case.<br /> It would mean Time loops would be impossible without other spheres.<br /> <br /> I think it's better explained in Revised (pg 193): &quot;By pulling time back into a loop, the mage causes a small area to suffer a local &quot;rewind&quot; of time. The mage herself remains immunized against this Effect due to her command of Time magic (otherwise he wouldn't know that he'd done anything and the looping would be almost pointless). From there, the mage can change her actions and responses to a given situation, already knowing how it would turn out otherwise. By combining life Life and Mind with the Effect, the mage can actually rewind herself physically and undo the effects of physical trauma, while still retaining her memory of the events that never happened.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T00:37:11-07:00","id":998639,"title":"","content":"I took the two to mean that in the first instance everyone can take new actions because the Mage just rewound time (essentially creating a set of new turns), where as with the Life 3 Mind 1 the Mage remembers how things are supposed to go and the others now follow their previous course of actions until the Mage intervenes (after which point it functions as new turns). In both cases the Mage can take new actions, its how the rest of the world proceeds as well that changes (basically whether or not the Mage has recollection of the exact course of events). Its not exactly the most clearly written section unfortunately, I see evidence for both arguments (although I am disinclined to try using previous editions, since not only do things change but certain wording may have been changed or omitted intentionally). As with most things, but especially with Time it comes down to ST adjudication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T01:49:28-07:00","id":998655,"title":"","content":"The others taking other actions implies they too are time travelling and remember a future that has happened. <br /> Because why should they take other actions if everything is as it was when they took action x? The only difference is the players of the others.<br /> <br /> By the way <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12551_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12551\" data-vbnamecard=\"12551\">artuard</a> you can go back days, years even. You only can't do it while in combat. Instead of one additional layer of dox per turn you receive one layer per section in the timetable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T02:37:18-07:00","id":998664,"title":"","content":"By the way <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12551_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12551\" data-vbnamecard=\"12551\">artuard</a> you can go back days, years even. You only can't do it while in combat. Instead of one additional layer of dox per turn you receive one layer per section in the timetable.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Yes you can go back further but when using the Time Sphere Timeline chart you get two times the layers in Paradox M20 pg 522 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a mage who travels backward according to the Time Sphere Timelines chart gets two layers of Paradox for each interval on that chart; going back 50 years (or four intervals), for example, nets eight times the usual amount of Paradox \u2013 eight points for each point normally earned. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T02:56:22-07:00","id":998670,"title":"","content":"I misremembered, gotta raise Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:46:34-07:00","id":998844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=997231#post997231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My head just exploded trying to think about this (I have my computer set to s