&amp;quot;Stop right there, criminal scum! We go first!&amp;quot;</i><br /> Big Bad Baddie: &amp;quot;Wait, where did you come fr-*Burninated*<br /> A Time Mage: <i>&amp;quot;Hmmmmh...&amp;quot;</i></div>Round 2:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>A Time Mage casts fireball</i></div>Round 3:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>A Time Mage casts fireball</i></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/09/7c/4d/097c4d14e4a5f4d1fd8a761b12cfe4da.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:40:28-07:00","id":998861,"title":"","content":"I think he meant that Justin Time has sent fireballs back in time to the first round before the big bad even began combat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T16:32:48-07:00","id":998940,"title":"","content":"Pfff, that would be the totally boring way to put it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:48:43-08:00","id":999194,"title":"","content":"so unless i have life and mind if i go back in time i cannot change the course of my action? i think mind alone should be enough i don't understand the life requirement.<br /> anyway time 3 alone then its no use for going back in time, since all u can do is just replay the same exact turn that already happened.<br /> <br /> EDIT- i'm dumb i re read your explanations guys and they make sense, thanks for pointing it out. i like the interpretation of cynic01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 11-06-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:52:52-08:00","id":999240,"title":"","content":"Yeah, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2008\" data-vbnamecard=\"2008\">Cynic01</a> makes it clear!<br /> <br /> On a bigger picture tho - there is a question if the rewind time/loop magic makes a small time bubble where things go back or is it a global back in time event. If it's global then why are the rest of time guys not feeling it or preventing it? If it's local ...then it indicates insane amount of time lines where each time mage opens another and another every time they do this effects..<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://static.fjcdn.com/gifs/Trippy+gif+3+different+gif+yet+still+mind+blowing_ba8bb2_3699999.gif\" target=\"_blank\">http://static.fjcdn.com/gifs/Trippy+...b2_3699999.gif</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:10:20-08:00","id":999250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=999240#post999240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2008\" data-vbnamecard=\"2008\">Cynic01</a> makes it clear!<br /> <br /> On a bigger picture tho - there is a question if the rewind time/loop magic makes a small time bubble where things go back or is it a global back in time event. If it's global then why are the rest of time guys not feeling it or preventing it? If it's local ...then it indicates insane amount of time lines where each time mage opens another and another every time they do this effects..<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://static.fjcdn.com/gifs/Trippy+gif+3+different+gif+yet+still+mind+blowing_ba8bb2_3699999.gif\" target=\"_blank\">http://static.fjcdn.com/gifs/Trippy+...b2_3699999.gif</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Best way I can describe that is an ocean analogy. Imagine time is like the Atlantic Ocean, your mage using Time 3 to loop time in a small area for a couple of turns makes is like someone splashing around on the beaches of the US, its not going to be noticed in the UK even though its technically in the same body of water. That said there is a reason for the greater difficulty, increased paradox, and the discussion of each additional Time effect in an area becoming more difficult; these all represent the splashing getting bigger, essentially Paradox means the Mage can almost never make a tsunami. However yes, Time Mages can detect the use of Time Magic and if they consistently notice an area with numerous anomalies they go to investigate (basically if your Mage is constantly rewinding Time and other tricks like that with little concern feel free to have another Time Mage, perhaps some Technocrats look into the anomalies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:10:20-08:00","id":999644,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2008\" data-vbnamecard=\"2008\">Cynic01</a> <br /> So the way you rule it is:<br /> Time 3: Everyone is aware that time has reversed, new actions can be done however they want.<br /> Time 3, Mind 3, Life 2: Only the time traveller is aware that time has reversed, and everyone will act as they had done unless changed<br /> <br /> I don't like that. It takes everything that's special about being a time traveller, being the only guy to know about what will happen and using your secret knowledge to aid in pinpoint ways, and throws it away.<br /> <br /> The way I saw it saw like this:<br /> <br /> Time 3: Only the time traveller is aware that time has reversed, and everyone will act as they had done unless changed.<br /> Extra successes can be used to &quot;extend&quot; the awareness of the time loop to other people (and if you really want, you can have a Mind requirement to target other mages minds)<br /> <br /> Time 3, Mind 3, Life 2: You can reverse time for your body, essentially healing yourself or reversing disease, without reversing your mind.<br /> To do this to other people, you may need Mind 4, Life 3.<br /> <br /> Similarly, other spheres can be used to reverse time for specific things rather than general things. You want to undo the draining of a node? Prime with Time 3. You want to return a damaged object to its original form? Mater with Time 3. You want to reverse the decaying process? Entropy with Time 3. You want see exactly where a bullet was shot from? Forces and Time 3.<br /> <br /> Regarding what range Time 3 effects, that depends on paradigm. If your mage sees time as a constant everywhere, then when they loop time, time is looped everywhere (though only sensed at the sight of casting). If your mage sees time as flexible and relative, then when they loop time it may only be in a localised area, in which case they'll need Corr 3 in order to reverse time for specific things.<br /> This is more of an optional rule that I like to use, where paradigm defines what the mage believes their spheres are capable off, and whether they need extra spheres or different levels to do the job. It makes things complicated, but I find it makes magic a bit more personalised, and drives players away from the Purple Paradigm.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12551_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12551\" data-vbnamecard=\"12551\">artuard</a> Remember, you're under no obligation to follow our interpretation. If you like Cynic01's account better than mine, then use it or hybrid them by all means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:39:36-08:00","id":999652,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> <br /> <br /> Time 3: Not everyone is aware time has reversed unless they have time magic but they might end up taking different actions; part of my logic comes from an earlier section in How do you do that pg 107 to 108<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Unpredictable Nature of Time<br /> To start with, treat time as an imprecise series of events whose results cannot be accurately understood. Every change to an event results in other changes to related events. And so, when a player uses Time magick to look backward, rewind time, or otherwise alter the timestream, the Storyteller can also use those events to retcon events in unpredictable ways. Sure, that Ecstatic weirdo thinks she can simply sidestep time to prevent a bullet from hitting her\u2026 and she can even succeed. When the events replay themselves, however, her would-be shooter picks another target instead, with results that she had not expected when she rewound time. Although the Storyteller should play fair with such variations, there\u2019s no reason that time should hop to the tune of a single character. Events and people, after all, are unpredictable, and not even a full Master of Time can accurately control what will happen, only assume what might happen. </div> </div> </div>Time 3 Life 3 Mind 1: Not only do they remember exactly what everyone else was doing they remember exactly what <i><b>they</b> </i>were doing. It means they wont cause the timeline to change ever so slightly because their arm was off by 45 degrees or their feet were in a slightly different spot or they turned their head to left instead of the right. They are exactly as they were in the first go through up moving exactly as they did their body in the same state until the exact moment they choose to change it. The section also provides a limit to the Reboot effect How do you do that pg 111 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Storyteller may declare that it\u2019s just not possible to reboot a character more than five turns into the past. Alternately, he could simply say, \u201cSure, you think you remember something about things having gone differently before, but everybody else remembers them going the way they\u2019re going now\u2026 so perhaps you DID go back in time, but this present is the result of your actions back then.\u201d </div> </div> </div> Five turns would be the max before that temporal drift from earlier seeps through even the mystical memory such is the nature of messing with time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:45:36-08:00","id":999654,"title":"","content":"Global time loops are not a good idea.<br /> Every mage (and certain other nightfolk) with time 1 can (and often will) try to counter it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:29:17-08:00","id":1003290,"title":"","content":"I actually understand the difference between a Time 3 &quot;Time Loop&quot; and a Time 3 Mind-sphere-requiring &quot;Reboot&quot; like this:<br /> <br /> * In the Time-Loop, the Mage themselves stay in place while their surroundings change back. The Mage themselves don't rewind, only the events around them.<br /> * In a Reboot, the Mage's body itself also rewinds, moving back into place where they were before - And to prevent the mind from re-setting in this case as well, the Mind sphere is needed.<br /> <br /> Now, why should anybody use the Reboot then, if it requires the Mind sphere?<br /> There are a few advantages:<br /> * Any damage and physical afflictions they caught during that time are healed, as their own body is also re-set.<br /> * Re-setting their own position and state makes sure that everything will happen exactly as it happened before, and how they remember it. Which is not a given in a Time-Loop, since the mage's position and physical state might be off, thus causing others around them to behave differently this time around.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Essentially what Cynic01 said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-15-2016, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:39:02-08:00","id":1003447,"title":"","content":"Interesting read on the Time Loops.<br /> <br /> Not to switch gears (so if this isn't the best thread, my apologies), but another blurry rule I am trying to understand involves Horizon Realms and Magickal Ratings<br /> <br /> Example (The Book of Chantries, pg. 35) : Magickal Ratings: Correspondence -2, Forces +4, Life +2, Matter -1, Mind +1, Prime +2<br /> <br /> 1) What exactly do these ratings mean?<br /> a) Are they Dice Pool modifiers?<br /> b) Are they TN modifiers?<br /> c) Are they success modifiers?<br /> d) Do they actually change the rank in your spheres?<br /> e) For conjuctional effects, do you apply best/worst/all?<br /> <br /> 2) Are they still valid in Mage 20th?<br /> <br /> 3) If so, are they talked about/determined anywhere?<br /> <br /> Examples involving mages that do / don't have those spheres would help.<br /> <br /> - Dan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T12:35:40-08:00","id":1003538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzizimine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=1003447#post1003447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example (The Book of Chantries, pg. 35) : Magickal Ratings: Correspondence -2, Forces +4, Life +2, Matter -1, Mind +1, Prime +2</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohh, that book is oooold. Like, First Edition old. Really old. Old old. Use it for fluff, but not for rules, I'd say.<br /> <br /> As for the Sphere ratings per realm in it, they are explained in the 1st Edition corebook of mage (Page 181), and...they *COULD* be valid in your Mage game, but are kind of an exotic mechanic:<br /> <br /> * Using Magick of a sphere that has an equal or lower rating than indicated by the number succeeds automatically, without a roll. We can already see how broken that is.<br /> * Using magick of a sphere rating that is higher than the number needs rolling and rules as usual.<br /> * The indicated number being negative actually means that even mundane tasks that fall under the sphere's purview would require magic to do. Example from the book: A realm with Correspondence -4 is essentially a 1-dimensional realm with two directions: Forward and back. Actually lifting something would *require* the use of Magick.<br /> <br /> Interesting, but broken due to the very first point already.<br /> <br /> <br /> My suggestion:<br /> If you want to use the ratings in a modern edition Mage game, switch the negative numbers to positive, and positive to negative. Treat them as difficulty modifiers from the base. I.e. Life +3 would *lessen* difficulty by 3.<br /> Remember that the max difficulty difference from base is +/-3, so in a realm with Matter 4, you would actually get 3 less difficulty for matter magick, but a situation that would bump the difficulty up by 1 from base still gets negated due to the 4 being one higher than the max of -3 difficulty from base..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-15-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T12:45:08-08:00","id":1003542,"title":"","content":"Thanks much. I hadn't seen the mechanic much since 1st Ed, but I never knew what they were used for. I probably would use something similar, but with probably no more than +/- 2. I assume with conjunctional effects, apply all, but still limited to the final modifier of +/- 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:50:47-08:00","id":1003618,"title":"","content":"I advice you not to calculate every possible modifier there is.<br /> In your case: don't look to much on the spheres involved. Use the sphere that is the most important of the effect.<br /> Essentially judge how good the effect fits in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T01:19:06-08:00","id":1003817,"title":"","content":"Yeah. For example, when conjuring a Fireball you need Forces+Prime, but basically the main focus of the effect is 'Fire'. Make fire. Hence, use the Forces difficulty modifier of the realm.<br /> <br /> That was also a good way to handle the old Revised One-Focus-Per-Sphere handling of instruments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:53:54-08:00","id":1003961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=1003817#post1003817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. For example, when conjuring a Fireball you need Forces+Prime, but basically the main focus of the effect is 'Fire'. Make fire. Hence, use the Forces difficulty modifier of the realm.<br /> <br /> That was also a good way to handle the old Revised One-Focus-Per-Sphere handling of instruments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this...<br /> Unless the theme of the realm is totally against ex nihilo effects. Then you should use the Prime difficulty modifier instead","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:30:17-08:00","id":1004090,"title":"","content":"That makes sense.<br /> <br /> Moving on to another blurry rule... Changes in Coincidence/Vulgarity After Casting?<br /> <br /> So, Joe Q. Mage casts Effect X at/on Target Y. The only requirements for Effect X are that is is long lasting (probably more than a scene, but definitely more than a single turn) and that Effect X starts off coincidental in one set of completely natural circumstances and would be vulgar (with or without witness) in another. There are no requirements for Target Y other than to support the duration of Effect X.<br /> <br /> Would Joe Q. Mage get paradox when Effect X, starting as coincidental, is revealed as vulgar?<br /> On a related note, would the change in vulgarity have an impact on successes already rolled?<br /> <br /> <b>Example 1: </b><br /> Joe just made a really elaborate sidewalk chalk drawing on a nice clear day on the boardwalk of his local beach. He's proud of it and wants it to stay intact while he gets his friends to come see. He weaves a coincidental Matter effect to make the chalk drawing impossible to be erased. The chalk becomes connected to the surface of the sidewalk. He gets enough successes for a whole day and gets on his bike and rides off to the bar down the street to get the gang, People walk on the chalk drawing, but it doesn't get scuffed or smudged and no one really notices or cares. <i>Effect: Coincidental</i><br /> <br /> About an hour after Joe leaves, a car driving on the boardwalk swerves to miss a pedestrian and crashes in a fire hydrant, which is now spraying water all over the chalk drawing.... which doesn't wash away even after prolonged exposure. <i>Effect: Vulgar with Witness</i>.<br /> <br /> Would Joe get paradox from the washing of his art project?<br /> <br /> Would Joe notice the change in vulgarity before the paradox hits, giving him a moment to dismiss his effect?<br /> <br /> Could Joe even dismiss his own effect, since he isn't near by when the vulgarity changes (assuming he doesn't have Correspondence at all) ?<br /> <br /> While it wouldn't really matter in this example, would the change in vulgarity effect the number of successes that Joe rolled back when it was still coincidental?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Example 2:</b><br /> Jane knows she is going into combat against some vampires and weaves a Life 3 effect to enhance her skin/muscle tissue/bones to make it impossible to breach the skin or break a bone, thus converting most kinds of lethal damage to bashing damage, thus soakable. Again, the duration lasts for a day (long enough for 2 scenes). During the first scene, she takes some punishment (stabs, claws, a gun shot), but ultimately she is goes down from breathing some toxin. One of her non-mage allies gets her out of combat and races to the hospital. <i>Effect: Coincidental or Vulgar without Witnesses</i><br /> <br /> At the hospital, the nurses manage to get Jane on an oxygen feed and begins filtering the toxins out, but are unable to get a needle into Jane's skin, since her protection effect is still preventing it. <i>Effect: Vulgar with Witnesses</i><br /> <br /> Would Jane get (more) paradox from the nurses witnessing the effect on her skin?<br /> <br /> Would the effect collapse because Jane is unconscious and it's being examined?<br /> <br /> If it collapses, would the wounds that Jane has already soaked as bashing become lethal? or would they stay bashing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12655,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","user":"tzizimine","date":". 11-17-2016, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T14:58:40-08:00","id":1004125,"title":"","content":"Sorry to load up, but another blurry question that came to mind just now involves trinkets, locking effects, extended rolls, and their effects in combat. (For those that have read the Dresden Files series, some of these will be familiar)<br /> <br /> <b>Example 1: </b>Joe Q. Mage wants to make a trench coat that is impossible to burn with regular fire (with the idea that whomever is wearing it would be resistant to fire).<br /> He weaves a Forces 2 only (or Forces 4 only, based on intensity) effect to make fire be repelled by the coat, but this would count as a sustained effect that Joe would have to maintain (counting towards that +1 / 2 effects modifier and would require the coat to stay in Joe's area of perception since he doesn't have Correspondence). The duration of the effect (and the protection it gives) would be based off of whatever successes he gets, probably using an extended ritual to get a really long duration (and if the Dividing Successes rule is used, to see the degree of protection).<br /> <br /> Just checking here, but Joe doesn't need to spend Quintessence for any of this? but the effect only lasts so long as the coat stays near him and he sustains it?<br /> <br /> <b>Example 2: </b>Joe Q. Mage wants to make a similar trench coat for his friend. This time, he weaves a Forces 2 / Matter 2 (or Forces 4 / Matter 4) to get the same effect, but lock it to the pattern of the coat. He doesn't count as being sustained. Same determination for successes, but now the coat can go with Joe's friend.<br /> <br /> Would this technically make the coat a <i>trinket</i> as per Corebook pg. 652?<br /> <br /> <b>Example 3: </b>Joe Q. Mage wants to make a magic bullet or a magic set of brass knuckles that will (hopefully) be a one-shot-one-kill, with a whole bunch of lethal (not aggravated) damage. He weaves a Forces 2 / Matter 2 (or Forces 4 / Matter 4) effect into the bullet or brass knuckles, with the idea that once fired (or a punch is thrown), all of the additional successes from an extended ritual stored as additional levels of damage assuming the attack hits the target (and the attack was made within the duration achieved, using the Divided Successes rule)<br /> <br /> Would this, in essence, be a one-use trinket?<br /> Would it need Quintessence (remember, lethal, not aggravated)?<br /> And would there be a limit to the number of magic bullets created (aside from the time for the ritual and duration of the effect)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T17:41:59-08:00","id":1004175,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12655\" data-vbnamecard=\"12655\">tzizimine</a><br /> <br /> My thoughts<br /> <br /> Example 1 (the chalk)<br /> The effect is not necessarily vulgar since there are ways to have waterproof chalk. If you think the water is too much/the force of it too powerful than it exceeds the parameters of the initial effect, veering from resistant to erasure to nearly impossible to erase at which point the drawing is erased because the chosen effect wasn't powerful enough to protect the chalk art (ie coincidental vs vulgar).<br /> <br /> Example 2 (Soaking Lethal)<br /> Vulgar without witness, and the needle wouldn't necessarily be prevented from entering. Often shrugging off damage makes what would be a fatal blow into a flesh wound. The needle goes through because its not 'damage' in the mechanical sense, this is because the effect you described was not her trying to make her skin bulletproof, but rather make bullet wounds less fatal. Wounds mitigated in this way remain bashing since they were already altered by the effect.<br /> <br /> Example 1 (fireproof coat)<br /> If he wants the coat itself to be repelling the Forces he needs Matter 2 to lock the effect to the coat, otherwise he is using a Forces effect around the area of the coat that he has to direct. If he locks it to the coat then the effect is probably coincidental so long as the coat appears as if it could be made of fireproof material (so a nice trenchcoat would whereas a battered one probably not). Also it would only protect the areas covered by the coat, so unless hes ducking down and pulling his head, hands, and feet in then those parts are still going to be burned otherwise the effect is vulgar since it is obviously pushing the flames away not merely resistant to them.<br /> <br /> Example 2 (Coat for a friend)<br /> It depends if you want the coat to actually repel the flames, or simply have extra soak vs flames<br /> <br /> Repel Flames - Wonder (Talisman) Prime 4 Forces 2 Matter 2, 10+ Quintessence<br /> This would be crafting a wonder (device or talisman) and would work as follows. You need Prime 4 in addition to Forces 2 . You need 5 quintessence to be infused into the object per dot of the wonder as well as 1 quintessence per roll made to craft it. Each dot represents a level of Sphere effect, Arete, and number of effects the item can have. So your Matter 2 Forces 2 effect would require 2 dots thus 10 quintessence. The wonder would have an Arete of 2 and 10 quintessence and would activate when a fire would affect it, rolling its Arete as a Forces 2 effect to repel the flames. Again the effect is likely coincidental if it would make sense that the jacket could be fireproof and the protection only applies to what the coat covers. (Similar to Bafflejack)<br /> <br /> Soak Dice - Wonder (Trinket) Prime 2 Forces 2 Matter 2, 10+ Quintessence<br /> If you wanted it to be a trinket (requiring only Prime 2 in addition to Forces 2 although still requiring 5 quintessence per Wonder dot and the 1 quintessence per roll made while crafting) you could have it grant soak dice vs Fire (again only applying to flames that the coat could appear to protect against), as a level 2 wonder you could have 3 dice to soak Fire damage (since its aggravated damage you can get 1 dice per 2 background points using the advantages chart as a guideline). (Similar to Bulletproof Hoodie)<br /> <br /> Example 3 (Discharge damage knuckles/bullet) - Wonder (Trinket) Prime 2 Forces 2 Matter 2, 10+ Quintessence<br /> A single use trinket that requires re-enchanting/is consumed by the use (knuckles/bullet) would require Prime 2 Forces 2 Matter 2 and 10 quintessence plus 1 per roll made while crafting. The item then contains the successes until it hits the target at which point the effect is expelled (remember that M20 suggests a cap of 20 health levels of damage on a Magickal attack). The limits on bullets is the available quintessence, time, and the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","user":"Cynic01","date":". 11-16-2016, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:37:43-08:00","id":1004378,"title":"","content":"Thanks for taking a look. I did edit the original post to remove some of the wiggle-room you pointed out. The intention of the scenarios was not to find the best way to narrowly avoid paradox, but see if the line between coincidental and vulgar changes overtime and, if so, what is the resulting paradox impact. <br /> <br /> In essence, if Joe Q Mage casts an effect that is coincidental in Scenario X and is sustained long enough to be in Scenario Y, where the effect is vulgar, when/does paradox hit? Would it get added like the way wards and paradox work from HDYDT?<br /> <br /> Or another way of asking is would the HAO/RBD check for coincidence / vulgar only happen at the point if casting or does stick around, 'watching' for the entire duration of the effect? If so, how is paradox handled when that check changes?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the trinket / wonder examples, I understand that it could be done with proper enchanting rules, but why would it need to be? The intention isn't for the coat, bullet or knuckles to stay that way for long, maybe a week or a month at most. Wouldn't locking an effect to the item without involving prime or enchanting rules be easier? I.e. is there some other benefit to proper enchanting vs. locking the effect that I am not seeing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:39:41-08:00","id":1004414,"title":"","content":"HDYDT states that <i>paradox only gets applied retroactively in the rarest of cases</i>.<br /> Pattern Bleeding, and similiar things, are examples of paradox troubles long after the spell has been cast. But usually, a paradox backlash only occurs on casting the effect.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean that I'd not use certain mechanics on the discovery of a clearly vulgar running effect by sleepers.<br /> I suggest this:<br /> An ST should keep track of the actual result of rolls that made up an effect, which can get potentially discovered by sleeprs as vulgar at a later time.<br /> <br /> Once the sleepers spot the IMPOSSIBLE THING, look at the rolls that were made, and raise the difficulty to Vulgar With Witness levels, which will usually reduce the successes of the effect.<br /> Does the effect still have enough duration left to sustain itself?<br /> If not, have it crumble and vanish under the weight of disbelief. Poof. This also kind of thematically mirrors the way that Bygones got/get purged over time by the consensus.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Last but not least, be critical of judging things as vulgar too quickly.<br /> Always ask yourself: 'How would I react in RL'.<br /> Example: How would <i>you</i> react in RL if you saw a chalk drawing, and a burst of water does not wash it away?<br /> I highly suspect you would simply think '<i>Oh neat, they are making waterproof chalk now</i>'. Or probably not even spend that much of a thought on it.<br /> <br /> Always, always consider your hypothetical mage-neutral subjective RL reaction first. We live in a time where technology and general belief in New Things Everyday does not only benefit the Technocracy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-17-2016, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T08:35:02-08:00","id":1004443,"title":"","content":"Thanks again, Ambrosia<br /> <br /> I kind of expected this is where we start get away from the complex RAW and into the even murkier RAI. I initially suspected that it might be handled like the wards section from HDYDT? where the paradox does occur but it doesn't risk a backlash roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:43:28-08:00","id":1004522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=1004414#post1004414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HDYDT states that <i>paradox only gets applied retroactively in the rarest of cases</i>.<br /> Pattern Bleeding, and similiar things, are examples of paradox troubles long after the spell has been cast. But usually, a paradox backlash only occurs on casting the effect.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean that I'd not use certain mechanics on the discovery of a clearly vulgar running effect by sleepers.<br /> I suggest this:<br /> An ST should keep track of the actual result of rolls that made up an effect, which can get potentially discovered by sleeprs as vulgar at a later time.<br /> <br /> Once the sleepers spot the IMPOSSIBLE THING, look at the rolls that were made, and raise the difficulty to Vulgar With Witness levels, which will usually reduce the successes of the effect.<br /> Does the effect still have enough duration left to sustain itself?<br /> If not, have it crumble and vanish under the weight of disbelief. Poof. This also kind of thematically mirrors the way that Bygones got/get purged over time by the consensus.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Last but not least, be critical of judging things as vulgar too quickly.<br /> Always ask yourself: 'How would I react in RL'.<br /> Example: How would <i>you</i> react in RL if you saw a chalk drawing, and a burst of water does not wash it away?<br /> I highly suspect you would simply think '<i>Oh neat, they are making waterproof chalk now</i>'. Or probably not even spend that much of a thought on it.<br /> <br /> Always, always consider your hypothetical mage-neutral subjective RL reaction first. We live in a time where technology and general belief in New Things Everyday does not only benefit the Technocracy...</div> </div> </div> </div>If the effect holds up, I ask if they want to maintain it. If yes they get Dox, if not the effect ceases to be. This option is only available if they are present in one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T12:17:17-08:00","id":1004571,"title":"","content":"Present being independently aware of the change in observation (i.e. still having the effect in their own area of perception or connected to it via Correspondence)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T15:01:18-08:00","id":1004660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tzizimine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=1004571#post1004571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Present being independently aware of the change in observation (i.e. still having the effect in their own area of perception or connected to it via Correspondence)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are viable. You could see it as a new casting without the need of spending an action and without a new Arete roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T21:47:27-08:00","id":1011847,"title":"","content":"So, another game mechanic question that I am having trouble untangling... And I realize that this will sound like min-maxing, but I can't see any reason not to do the following.<br /> <br /> Any mystic character concept you like; Arete 3; paradigm, practice, 7 instruments of your choice; and the instrument you choose to discard for gaining the third dot of Arete is as versatile as your practice can allow (language, thought forms, etc)<br /> <br /> Is there any GAME-MECHANIC reason why that mage wouldn't use that specific instrument for all of their effects, getting the -1 TN for using an instrument you don't need?<br /> <br /> I realize that there are plenty of STORY reasons that you shouldn't X instrument for Y effects, but no game mechanics for enforcing it. And, more importantly, no precedent for setting the requirements from the story reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T05:35:00-08:00","id":1011958,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately you are right.<br /> No Mechanics prohibit this. It is the same as Paradigm: nothing RAW forces you to select a narrow Paradigm.<br /> Dataweaver has a easy homebrew solution:<br /> You don't need instruments if your Arete is at least twice the effect level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T06:15:33-08:00","id":1011981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=1011958#post1011958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately you are right.<br /> No Mechanics prohibit this. It is the same as Paradigm: nothing RAW forces you to select a narrow Paradigm.<br /> Dataweaver has a easy homebrew solution:<br /> You don't need instruments if your Arete is at least twice the effect level.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons why I disregard the &quot;build-a-paradigm&quot; approach M20 goes for in favour of a more personalised &quot;how does the universe work in your mage's mind&quot; philosophical musings approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T06:20:02-08:00","id":1011984,"title":"","content":"I see. Thanks for clarification. I'll take a look at these other options you mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T09:28:22-08:00","id":1012038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997085-some-questions-on-blurry-rules?p=1011981#post1011981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is one of the reasons why I disregard the &quot;build-a-paradigm&quot; approach M20 goes for in favour of a more personalised &quot;how does the universe work in your mage's mind&quot; philosophical musings approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that work out in actual game play? Does the game become even more of an extended philosophical sparring match between a particular player and the ST over pretty much every casting? (With the play effect of sidelining every other player....) How does that even manifest?<br /> <br /> That's one reason finally having some real concrete paradigm in play utility rules (aka Focus) were, IMHO, one of the major contributions of M20. Now we don't have to stumble over the whole player part of describing their part of the casting as it was previously. Now they know they have to give an explanation of what their character is DOING in-game to make the magic happen. <br /> <br /> E.g. We have two characters in my current Mage group that have Mind 3 &amp; the Correspondence to use it beyond of line of sight. One is NWO CSI and the other is a Cultist transcendentalist rustic poet. In the most recent session, the player of the NWO said, &quot;I want to set up a telepathic network with the other members of the group.&quot; So there was a brief navel-gazing discussion that was focused on the practical mechanics of how that worked vis-a-vis his Focus, which ventured into how that would, or even could, work as a possible effect for his character. Since he is usually reading people's minds by making deductions from kinesics and proximics, often prompted by eliciting responses by his statements, tone, postures, etc. He posited he could do it using the ear buds created by another PC. The question was still &quot;How does that work, if he needs to not just hear, but see and also interact with the target?&quot; The answer was that he couldn't really do that as things were set up. (Which led to a later discussion between the NWO character and the tech support character about making the &quot;ear buds&quot; do more than just transmit/receive noise and maybe transmit a neural map to the NWO's new tablet to allow him greater insight combined with his understanding of tone, word choice, etc. that would be the telepathic-reciever part of the &quot;mass mind link&quot; effectand he could just use his typical super-innuedo voice to get his thoughts across to the others.... These neural mapping ear buds are on the tech-guy's To-do list.) <br /> <br /> He ended up just asking the Cultist to do it. Which was much closer to effortless. Previously, the Cultist had drawn pictures of each character in his journal and had them sign them. He had made 5 pics of himself, signed them, tore the page out and up into 5 pieces and gave one to each of them. When asked to set up the telepathic link, he opened up his journal to the page and made up a poem about them, listening to the whispering wind, mutual understanding, etc. (No, the player didn't make up the poem, but, sometimes she does create a few lines on the spot.... typically gets a -1 Diff for that effort). Wham! Telepathic links all around. <br /> <br /> Note: Most of the discussion (which took less time to have than it has taken me to type it) wasn't about how the character's perceive magic, particularly as a philosophical construct. There was some of that for the NWO PC, but much of it was implicit rather than explicit. The vast majority of the discussion was about how doing all that looked in the world, what the characters put into doing their magic, etc. That's one of the benefits of the M20 Focus system. Sure, we did that to one degree or another beforehand (sometimes, often it was just wishcrafting reality, particularly back in 1st Ed days), but now we have an actual structure to inform those discussions and make them material and meaningful when actually playing the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T10:41:11-08:00","id":1012067,"title":"","content":"That is helpful, and once gameplay has started, it makes sense, but it leaves the question(s) that come up from the create-you-own-paradigm/practice (CYOPP) at character creation about which Instruments to choose and when the benefit of working without instruments from higher Arete applies.<br /> <br /> The house rule that I have been working on goes like this.<br /> <br /> Every practice has X number of instruments (default 7, but I'm considering 9). Each instrument covers one from a set list of categories and is the instrument that counts when the primary aspect of that effect falls into that category. All Instruments must align the mage's chosen practice.<br /> <br /> (See below for category idea)<br /> <br /> At least X/3, round down (so 2 or 3 for 7 or 9 respectively) need to be things the mage DOES, represented by an Ability.<br /> <br /> At least X/3, round down, need to be things that the mage HAS, being a physical item (or items) the mage has.<br /> <br /> The remaining can be either Ability or Item.<br /> <br /> For Ability Instruments, the rank in that Ability must be equal to or greater than the rank of the highest sphere used) and the Ability must be able to be used at the time of casting. If the Ability is a secondary Ability (meaning the Ability itself won't see much dice rolling), it counts as a Unique Instrument (standard -1 to TN).<br /> <br /> For Item Instruments, the item has to be unique, complicated or delicate enough that replacing it or repairing it takes a week of effort and the item(s) have to be present and in the possession of the mage at the time of casting. If the item is unique, complicated or delicate enough that replacing or repairing it takes a month or more, or its own side quest, it counts as Unique.<br /> <br /> Each instrument (Ability or Item) has its own recommended amount of time needed to be used appropriately as well as whether or not they are suitable for extended rolls or ritual work. Using instruments too quickly or inappropriately causes the appropriate penalties to the TN.<br /> <br /> Examples<br /> <br /> Computer: 1 minute, Ritual: Yes<br /> Drive: 1 combat turn, Ritual: No<br /> Firearms: 1 combat turn, Ritual: No<br /> Intimidation: 1 minute: Ritual: No<br /> Meditation: 1 minute, Ritual: Yes<br /> Technology: 1 hour, Ritual: Yes<br /> <br /> Art (drawing, music, quick sketch): 1 minute, Ritual: Yes<br /> Art (other): 1 hour, Ritual: Yes<br /> Media: 1 hour, Ritual: Yes<br /> Social Dominion: 1 minute, Ritual: Yes<br /> Melee Weapons: 1 turn (combat, 6 seconds), Ritual: Yes<br /> Vocalization: 1 turn (combat, 6 seconds)<br /> <br /> <br /> The category issue...<br /> In 1st Ed, the categories were obvious. 9 categories, 1 for each sphere. The highest sphere or the one primarily responsible for the effect would be the one that counts for this idea. But not all groups use the sphere model (Kopa Loei for example).<br /> <br /> Another category list could just be the general purposes of the effect, like<br /> <br /> Offensive<br /> Defensive<br /> Restorative<br /> Transportation<br /> Alteration<br /> Perception<br /> Communication<br /> Control<br /> Creation<br /> <br /> This works a little better, but I am concerned it is not an exhaustive list.<br /> <br /> The end goal is that the benefit of higher Arete goes toward a specific subset of effects, that subset grows as the Arete increases until Arete 10 covers all effects and that the Instruments chosen have a clear impact on time requirements.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12655,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","user":"tzizimine","date":". 12-04-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T11:53:53-08:00","id":1012091,"title":"","content":"Great work!<br /> But I fear your categories are unbalanced because the offense/defense pair is way broader than the others.<br /> Minor nitpicks: Driving for drivings sake is done by motorcyclists, why shouldn't a mage get ritual castings (plus imagine a biker cult).<br /> Zen Archery is a thing why not Gun Fu rituals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:35:00-08:00","id":1012109,"title":"","content":"The specifics on the instrument list isn't anywhere close to complete but all of those could work. The offensive/defensive pairing would be limited to dealing / preventing damage (or making it easier). If anything, Alteration would be the broadest, covering everything from Better Body to rewriting memories to Transformer cars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T00:04:41-08:00","id":1012425,"title":"","content":"Sounds better with that in mind.<br /> Alteration should then be split, Better body and other improvements should be Perfecting, or should go to Restorative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T03:45:34-08:00","id":1012476,"title":"","content":"Going back to time travel briefly, one of the things that crops up in popular culture is multiple copies of a person. So when you go back, there's your present self and past self in that same point in time. <br /> <br /> Under that logic, Time 3 would be travelling bodily back in time and so creating two versions of yourself. Time 3 Life 3 Mind 1 would allow you just to transport your mind back into your past body, so there would only be one version of yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:13:34-08:00","id":1012504,"title":"","content":"Or it is the problem of sphere linking/Paradigm<br /> If you think along Time and Correspondence, then you get 1 Timetraveller.<br /> If you think Spacetime, then obviously you get 2 Timetravellers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}